        "original_id": "97ed733d-4859-5a6a-aba1-5919dfb68d99",
        "text": "This chunk is about:\n- People: Rosario Castellanos, Lucy Maud Montgomery, Jean-Claude Andro, Carlos Fuentes, Anne Shirley\n- Places: Mexico, Canada, Prince Edward Island, Avonlea\n- Works: Anne of Green Gables, Zone sacrée, Chant des aveugles, Christ des ténèbres, Road to Avonlea\n- Roles: poet, author, novelist, translator\n\nFacts:\n- Lucy Maud Montgomery was born on November 30, 1874, and she was a Canadian author published as L.M. Montgomery.\n- Rosario Castellanos Figueroa was born on May 25, 1925, and she was a Mexican poet and author.\n- In 1908, Lucy Maud Montgomery began her best-known novel series with Anne of Green Gables.\n- Jean-Claude Andro pursued a career as a novelist and translator.\n- Jean-Claude Andro translated Zone sacrée and Chant des aveugles by Carlos Fuentes and Christ des ténèbres by Rosario Castellanos.\n- Avonlea is a fictional community on Prince Edward Island, Canada.\n- Avonlea is the setting of Lucy Maud Montgomery's Anne of Green Gables and its sequels, which follow Anne Shirley.\n- Avonlea is also the setting of the television series Road to Avonlea.\n- Lucy Maud Montgomery died on April 24, 1942.\n- Rosario Castellanos Figueroa died on August 7, 1974.",
        "type": "TextSummary"
      },
      {
        "id": 1,
        "original_id": "b286a03b-a97a-5456-9d13-5e726cbe0eff",
        "text": "Page: Rosario Castellanos. Sentence: Rosario Castellanos Figueroa (] ; 25 May 1925 – 7 August 1974) was a Mexican poet and author.\nPage: Lucy Maud Montgomery. Sentence: Lucy Maud Montgomery {'1': \", '2': \", '3': \", '4': \"} (November 30, 1874 – April 24, 1942) published as L.M. Montgomery, was a Canadian author best known for a series of novels beginning in 1908 with \"Anne of Green Gables\".\nPage: Jean-Claude Andro. Sentence: He then pursued a career as a novelist and translator (\"Zone sacrée\" and \"Chant des aveugles\" by Carlos Fuentes and \"Christ des ténèbres\" by Rosario Castellanos).\nPage: Avonlea (Anne of Green Gables). Sentence: Avonlea ( ;\"ah-von-LEE\") is a fictional community located on Prince Edward Island, Canada, and is the setting of Lucy Maud Montgomery's novel \"Anne of Green Gables\", following the adventures of Anne Shirley, as well as its sequels, and the television series \"Road to Avonlea\".",
        "type": "DocumentChunk"
      },
